        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. One dead, five wounded after shootings in Israel Middle East Issued on: 07/06/2026 - 16:18 A Palestinian man with Israeli citizenship went on a shooting rampage in several towns in central Israel on Sunday, killing one person and wounding five others, according to Israeli police. The attacker was killed by police. The attack came at a time of heightened tensions following a spate of Israeli settler attacks, and the deadly shooting of a Palestinian baby over the weekend, in the nearby West Bank. Police identified the attacker as a resident of the nearby Arab town of Taybeh in his 20s, but his precise motives were not immediately known. One killed, five wounded in terror attacks in Israel 07/06/2026 Middle East Israeli troops kill infant, injure parents in West Bank 07/06/2026 Middle East 07/06/2026 Middle East Several soldiers killed in Israeli strike on Lebanon 06/06/2026 Middle East Annual Jerusalem Pride parade marches to Knesset to demand legislative change, equal rights 04/06/2026 Middle East Lebanon health ministry says Israeli strikes in south and east kill eight 04/06/2026 Middle East A 'ceasefire war' in Lebanon continues as 'chaotic global leadership' takes its toll 04/06/2026 Middle East Kuwait releases footage of drone strike on airport 04/06/2026 Middle East 'US war on Iran not about the Iranian people: Europe can put the issue of human rights on the table' 03/06/2026 Middle East"
